<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="ws-exponential-graphs-to-equations">
  <title>Exponential Models: Graphs to Equations</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Exponential models have form <m>f(x)=ab^x</m>, where <m>a</m> is the initial value and <m>b</m> is the growth or decay factor.</p>
    <p>Given a percent change <m>r</m>, find <m>b</m> by adding or subtracting <m>r</m> from 1 based on whether it is a percent increase or decrease.</p>
  </introduction>

  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="expgraph-q1">
      <introduction>
        <p>Consider the following graph of an exponential function:</p>
        <image width="65%">
          <shortdescription>Graph of a decaying exponential curve on a coordinate grid.</shortdescription>
          <description>
            <p>
              A coordinate grid with the <m>x</m>-axis running from -2 to 4 and the <m>y</m>-axis running from -18 to 2, gridlines every 1 unit horizontally and every 2 units vertically.
              A curve starts near the top left, decreases steeply, and flattens as it approaches the <m>x</m>-axis from below. The curve passes through the points
              <m>(-1,-16)</m>, <m>(0,-8)</m>, <m>(1,-4)</m>, <m>(2,-2)</m>, and <m>(3,-1)</m>.
            </p>
          </description>
          <prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="expgraph-q1-fig">
            <diagram dimensions="(400,360)" margins="(35,30,15,15)">
              <definition>f(x) = -8*(0.5)^x</definition>
              <coordinates bbox="(-2,-18,4,2)">
                <grid-axes xlabel="x" ylabel="y"
                  hspacing="(-2,1,4)" hlabels="(-2,1,4)"
                  vspacing="(-18,2,2)" vlabels="(-18,2,2)"/>
                <graph function="f" stroke="blue" thickness="2"/>
              </coordinates>
            </diagram>
          </prefigure>
        </image>
      </introduction>
      <task xml:id="expgraph-q1-a">
        <statement>
          <p>Fill in the table of values based on the graph.</p>
          <tabular>
            <row header="yes">
              <cell>x</cell>
              <cell>-1</cell>
              <cell>0</cell>
              <cell>1</cell>
              <cell>2</cell>
              <cell>3</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>y</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
        </statement>
      </task>
      <task xml:id="expgraph-q1-b" workspace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>Write an equation for this exponential function in <m>y=ab^x</m> form.</p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>

</worksheet>
